```text
ReduceCliqueToIndependentSet(G, k):
    H <- graph with vertex set V(G) and no edges
    for each unordered pair {u, v} with u != v:
        if {u, v} not in E(G):
            add edge {u, v} to E(H)
    return (H, k)
```
The construction makes $H = \overline{G}$. A set $S$ of size $k$ is a clique in $G$ iff no two vertices of $S$ are adjacent in $H$, so $S$ is an independent set in $H$.
